87
00:03:12,791 --> 00:03:14,598
At four per cent, about nineteen.

88
00:03:15,382 --> 00:03:17,389
At six per cent, about twenty-seven,

89
00:03:17,892 --> 00:03:20,362
and at seven per cent, nearly thirty-nine.

90
00:03:21,085 --> 00:03:23,488
So a rate rise of one point adds

91
00:03:23,529 --> 00:03:25,933
about five years, but a fall of one

92
00:03:25,974 --> 00:03:27,676
point saves only about three.

93
00:03:28,681 --> 00:03:29,124
Here's why.

94
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:33,135
A higher rate raises the interest-only line, so

95
00:03:33,256 --> 00:03:35,219
less of the same repayment is left for

96
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:35,680
the debt.

97
00:03:36,282 --> 00:03:37,906
And the closer that line gets to your

98
00:03:37,947 --> 00:03:40,091
repayment, the faster the term grows.

99
00:03:40,854 --> 00:03:43,441
This matters most for someone paying the thirty-year

100
00:03:43,483 --> 00:03:44,003
repayment.

101
00:03:44,626 --> 00:03:46,266
With a rate fixed at six per cent

102
00:03:46,307 --> 00:03:48,748
from the start, paying two thousand one hundred

103
00:03:48,769 --> 00:03:51,790
and forty-seven dollars twenty-nine stretches the term to

104
00:03:51,971 --> 00:03:53,331
almost forty-five years.

105
00:03:54,213 --> 00:03:55,455
At six and a half per cent, the

106
00:03:55,496 --> 00:03:57,860
first month's interest is two thousand one hundred

107
00:03:57,881 --> 00:03:59,745
and sixty-six dollars sixty-seven.

108
00:04:00,327 --> 00:04:03,073
That's more than the repayment, so the balance

109
00:04:03,134 --> 00:04:05,319
grows, and the loan is never repaid.

110
00:04:06,182 --> 00:04:08,347
A loan only shrinks when the repayment is

111
00:04:08,488 --> 00:04:10,052
more than the interest on the balance.

112
00:04:10,842 --> 00:04:12,150
Here's the idea in one line.

113
00:04:12,833 --> 00:04:15,263
Only what's left after the interest pays the

114
00:04:15,284 --> 00:04:15,846
loan down.

115
00:04:16,610 --> 00:04:18,079
A bigger repayment leaves more.

116
00:04:18,804 --> 00:04:20,352
A higher rate leaves less.

117
00:04:21,055 --> 00:04:23,359
And if nothing's left, the loan never shrinks.

118
00:04:26,214 --> 00:04:26,662
